      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ed9ff046-f0f3-5ee4-9361-e82ef037b688",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Coolio, Stevie Wonder\n- Products: Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits, It Takes a Thief, Gangsta's Paradise, My Soul, Pastime Paradise, Curtain Falls\n- Concepts: compilation albums, sampling\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Stevie Wonder released the song \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- In 1995, Coolio released the hit \"Gangsta's Paradise,\" which samples the chorus and instrumentation of Stevie Wonder's 1976 song \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- The background music of \"Curtain Falls\" is almost identical to that of Coolio's \"Gangsta's Paradise\" because both songs use a sample of Stevie Wonder's \"Pastime Paradise.\"\n- In 2001, Coolio released the compilation album \"Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits.\"\n- Songs on \"Fantastic Voyage: The Greatest Hits\" originally appeared on Coolio's first three albums: \"It Takes a Thief,\" \"Gangsta's Paradise,\" and \"My Soul.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
